Most of the song is just barre chords, D(5th fret) to C(3rd fret) with your pinky out on the
fourth string on the 7th fret, to a normal barre C, to an A on the fifth fret.  Almost the entire song is that chord
progression played differently.  When he says, "I miss the innocence I've known" I've heard him play different stuff.
This is what I like to play for that section.  I don't think he ever plays it exactly like this but it?s close to several versions
I've heard.  And close enough, in my opinion. However, always eager for any additions or corrections.

